**/__pycache__/
**/*.pth
**/*.npz
# ...EXCEPT the fitted SPS bands of rounds that actually scored. A band is the one part of a
# package that is NOT reproducible from the checkpoints: `base` is 81 920 per-element
# half-widths fitted by sps9.optimal_band on the held-out twins' error field, and refitting
# with a different twin set or window order gives a different table. They are 0.5 MB each and
# there are seven distinct ones across sixteen scored rounds, so version control is the right
# home; the blanket rule above exists for the 1 GB of derived val_*.npz caches, which rebuild
# from the h5 in minutes. Round 18 shipped a pricing run against a STALE band because nothing
# recorded which file a build had produced -- `git log Track_1/bands/` is that record now.
!Track_1/bands/*.npz
**/*.pt
**/*.zip
**/*.log
# build artefacts: staged package directories are reproduced by build_zip.py / build_t2.py
Track_1/submit_fno/_package*/
Track_2/_pkg/
*.bak
# Slurm writes slurm-<jobid>.out into the SUBMIT directory, which is the repo root when a
# job is queued from here. The logs belong in $SCRATCH/logs, never in a commit.
slurm-*.out
leaderboard/index.html
